      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1890, the town was founded as Bonito when several Hispanic families made a deal with a cattle agent to settle here.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrey%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1901, and the settlement was renamed for its first postmaster, Urbano Arrey, a homesteader.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/arrey_new_mexico",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The San Jose Catholic Mission was founded in 1891, reflecting the community's early Hispanic cultural roots and providing an enduring religious center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/arrey_new_mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Arrey lies within the Chihuahuan Desert ecoregion, where drought‑resistant shrubs, cacti, and riparian cottonwood trees thrive along the Rio Grande.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/arrey_new_mexico",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The local economy centers on farming, with crops like chili peppers, cotton, onions, pumpkins, and alfalfa sustaining the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrey%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
